  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Flood Disaster in Ethiopia, Somalia, and Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The prolonged drought from 2020 to 2023 with sixth failed rainy seasons severely impacted the population in Arid and Semi-Arid Land (ASAL) region of Kenya with over 5.4 million people facing acute food insecurity, of which 1.2 million people are in Emergency level by Integrated Food Security Phase Classification (IPC). In response to the worsening condition of the mobile and most vulnerable population severely impacted by flooding, IOM seeks to provide emergency shelters and non-food items (NFIs) to alleviate the suffering of the most vulnerable households affected by the recent flooding across the affected ASAL counties.</narrative>
  </description>
